{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0116TKjmXqJS6jmQ4kXvLoWF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"14B Clean FP16 Scale Validation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-14B FP16 (无量化) on 96GB RTX PRO 6000。Nucleus p=0.95，d0-d3 递归 LoRA  fine-tuning 链。Pythia-1.4B reference model 提取 19 维统计特征。RF/LR 5-fold CV。 Binary pairwise d0-d5 确定 EDD。验证 depth signal 在 14B 规模是否持续。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"rf_4class_acc\": 0.76,\n7\t      \"rf_4class_ci\": [\n8\t        0.745,\n9\t        0.775\n10\t      ],\n11\t      \"lr_4class_acc\": 0.72,\n12\t      \"lr_4class_ci\": [\n13\t        0.705,\n14\t        0.735\n15\t      ],\n16\t      \"rf_3class_acc\": 0.71,\n17\t      \"rf_3class_ci\": [\n18\t        0.692,\n19\t        0.728\n20\t      ],\n21\t      \"pairwise_auc_rf\": {\n22\t        \"d0v1\": 0.988,\n23\t        \"d0v2\": 0.997,\n24\t        \"d0v3\": 0.999,\n25\t        \"d1v2\": 0.87,\n26\t        \"d1v3\": 0.975,\n27\t        \"d2v3\": 0.79\n28\t      },\n29\t      \"per_class_recall\": {\n30\t        \"d0\": 0.97,\n31\t        \"d1\": 0.82,\n32\t        \"d2\": 0.58,\n33\t        \"d3\": 0.72\n34\t      },\n35\t      \"per_class_f1\": {\n36\t        \"d0\": 0.96,\n37\t        \"d1\": 0.81,\n38\t        \"d2\": 0.6,\n39\t        \"d3\": 0.7\n40\t      },\n41\t      \"top_features\": [\n42\t        \"p90_ppl (0.19)\",\n43\t        \"var_surprisal (0.16)\",\n44\t        \"p75_ppl (0.11)\",\n45\t        \"mean_surprisal (0.09)\",\n46\t        \"mean_ppl (0.07)\"\n47\t      ],\n48\t      \"feature_overlap_with_1b_top2\": 2,\n49\t      \"finetune_losses\": {\n50\t        \"depth_0\": 1.95,\n51\t        \"depth_1\": 1.25,\n52\t        \"depth_2\": 0.92\n53\t      },\n54\t      \"binary_pairwise_auc\": {\n55\t        \"d1v2\": 0.93,\n56\t        \"d2v3\": 0.86,\n57\t        \"d3v4\": 0.76,\n58\t        \"d4v5\": 0.69\n59\t      },\n60\t      \"edd_at_075\": 4,\n61\t      \"code_contamination_narrow_max\": 0.02\n62\t    },\n63\t    \"tables\": [\n64\t      \"Table 2: Scale validation — Qwen2.5-14B row alongside 3×1B models (4-class acc, d1v2 AUC, EDD)\",\n65\t      \"Table S2: 14B per-class precision/recall/F1 + binary pairwise AUC for EDD determination\"\n66\t    ],\n67\t    \"figures\": [],\n68\t    \"analysis\": \"14B 结果直接启用 Claim 1 中 \\\"1B-14B scale robustness\\\" 子句。76% 是 chance (25%) 的 3 倍， 确认 ordinal depth signal 在主流模型规模持续存在且无需量化（消除 7B QLoRA 矛盾结果的干扰）。 Feature universality 现在覆盖 4 个模型家族、10+ settings——论文最强实证发现。 EDD=4 跨尺度一致性将 Atlas 从 \\\"1B-only observation\\\" 升级为 \\\"scale-invariant structural  property of recursive generation\\\"。~4pp 下降是预期中的且可解释（larger model, slower collapse）， 不是弱点而是支撑 tail erosion 理论的额外证据。\\n\\n\\n14B 模型容量 ~10x 于 1B，每步递归 fine-tuning 产生的分布偏移更小（更强的模型更接近地复制训练数据）， 导致 per-step 特征差异压缩。这解释了 ~4pp 的准确率下降（76% vs 1B nucleus 均值 80.1%）。\\n但 tail erosion 机制 (Shumailov 2024) 是 scale-invariant 的：递归训练在有限样本上系统性地 under-represent 低概率事件，与模型大小无关。因为采样过程本身截断了真实分布的尾部——无论模型多大， 从有限样本 fine-tune 都会丢失 tail events。p90_ppl 直接度量这种 tail contraction（每步递归 第 90 百分位 per-token perplexity 下降），var_surprisal 捕获 surprisal 分布随分布集中向 mode  的收窄。两者在 14B 仍然 top-2/3 是因为度量的是文本分布属性而非模型架构属性。\\nEDD=4 匹配 1B 是因为：更大模型的更慢收缩率被 reference model (Pythia-1.4B) 对更精细分布差异的 同样降低的敏感度所抵消——14B d3 和 d4 的差异更微妙，但 Pythia 对 14B 生成文本的基线敏感度也更低 （domain shift），两个效应大致相消，使得 AUC=0.75 阈值在同一相对位置（depth 4）被达到。\\nd3v4 AUC 0.76（刚过阈值）反映 depth 4 的信号仍可检测但微弱；d4v5 0.69 跌破阈值，符合几何收敛 到 attractor 的预期。d2 recall 最低 (0.58) 与 1B 模式一致——d2 被夹在 d1 和 d3 之间， 是最难区分的 depth class。\\n\"\n69\t  },\n70\t  {\n71\t    \"name\": \"Wild-data Calibration (C4/FineWeb/RedPajama)\",\n72\t    \"description\": \"系统化 wild-data 评估。用 Pythia/OLMo/GPT-2 XL 三个 reference model 分别提取 19 特征， 在 C4、FineWeb、RedPajama 各 10K passages 上用 3×3 训练好的 RF 分类器做 depth 预测。 分析 depth 分布、FPR 模式、跨 reference model 一致性。\\n\",\n73\t    \"results\": {\n74\t      \"c4\": {\n75\t        \"n_passages\": 10000,\n76\t        \"d0_pct_mean\": 72.0,\n77\t        \"d0_pct_range_across_ref\": [\n78\t          66.0,\n79\t          95.3\n80\t        ],\n81\t        \"d1_pct_mean\": 22.0,\n82\t        \"d2_pct_mean\": 3.5,\n83\t        \"d3_pct_mean\": 2.5,\n84\t        \"fpr_mean\": 28.0,\n85\t        \"fpr_range_across_ref\": [\n86\t          4.7,\n87\t          34.0\n88\t        ],\n89\t        \"cross_model_d0_agreement_pct\": 88\n90\t      },\n91\t      \"fineweb\": {\n92\t        \"n_passages\": 10000,\n93\t        \"d0_pct_mean\": 82.0,\n94\t        \"d0_pct_range_across_ref\": [\n95\t          78.0,\n96\t          88.0\n97\t        ],\n98\t        \"d1_pct_mean\": 15.5,\n99\t        \"d2_pct_mean\": 1.5,\n100\t        \"d3_pct_mean\": 1.0,\n101\t        \"fpr_mean\": 18.0,\n102\t        \"fpr_range_across_ref\": [\n103\t          12.0,\n104\t          22.0\n105\t        ],\n106\t        \"cross_model_d0_agreement_pct\": 91\n107\t      },\n108\t      \"redpajama\": {\n109\t        \"n_passages\": 10000,\n110\t        \"d0_pct_mean\": 81.0,\n111\t        \"d0_pct_range_across_ref\": [\n112\t          76.0,\n113\t          90.0\n114\t        ],\n115\t        \"d1_pct_mean\": 15.0,\n116\t        \"d2_pct_mean\": 2.5,\n117\t        \"d3_pct_mean\": 1.5,\n118\t        \"fpr_mean\": 19.0,\n119\t        \"fpr_range_across_ref\": [\n120\t          10.0,\n121\t          24.0\n122\t        ],\n123\t        \"cross_model_d0_agreement_pct\": 89\n124\t      },\n125\t      \"editorial_text_fpr\": \"<3%\",\n126\t      \"template_content_fpr\": \"35-50%\",\n127\t      \"cross_model_rank_corr_d0_pct\": 0.82,\n128\t      \"olmo_systematic_lowest_fpr\": true\n129\t    },\n130\t    \"tables\": [\n131\t      \"Table 5: Wild-data depth distributions — corpus × reference model (3×3 grid)\",\n132\t      \"Table S5: FPR breakdown by content type (editorial vs template vs SEO), with examples\"\n133\t    ],\n134\t    \"figures\": [],\n135\t    \"analysis\": \"Wild-data calibration 弥合 controlled→ecological validity 的最后一步。分类器在真实语料上 行为连贯：高质量文本→d0，template 内容→d1，无虚假 d2/d3。支撑 Discussion 中  \\\"depth-graduated curation\\\" 论点。论文表述：\\\"our classifier exhibits meaningful behavior on  uncurated web text, correctly separating editorial from template-generated content, though  definitive depth labels are unavailable for wild data.\\\"\\n\\n\\n已有 wild-data 实验已建立核心模式：编辑质量高的文本 (WikiText, OpenWebText) FPR <3%， web-crawl (C4, FineWeb) FPR 15-34%。三模型系统化分析确认这不是单一 reference model 的 artifact。\\nFPR 差异的根因已确认：web-crawl 语料中 15-30% 是 template/SEO/机器翻译内容，这些文本与 模型生成文本共享统计指纹（高重复率、压缩的 perplexity tail、低词汇多样性）。这不是真正的  false positive——分类器正确识别了具有 \\\"shallow synthetic\\\" 特征的文本。\\nOLMo 系统性 FPR 最低（已确认：C4 4.72% vs Pythia 20.2%/GPT-2 XL 22.4%），因为 OLMo  d1-d3 特征与 d0 的差异更大，产生更宽的 d0 决策边界。GPT-2 XL FPR 最高因为信号最强—— d0 和 d1 的 feature gap 更小，导致 template 内容更容易落入 d1 范围。\\nCross-model d0 agreement ~88-91% 意味着三个 reference model 对同一段 passage 的 d0/non-d0 判断高度一致，确认信号在文本本身而非 reference model 的偏差。d1-heavy 分布（vs d2/d3 近零） 符合预期：大多数 \\\"synthetic-looking\\\" web 文本类似浅层模型输出，不是深度递归文本。\\nFineWeb 和 RedPajama 的 FPR 低于 C4 反映了各自的质量过滤：FineWeb 有激进的去重和质量过滤， RedPajama 混合了 Wikipedia/books/ArXiv 等高质量源。\\n\"\n136\t  },\n137\t  {\n138\t    \"name\": \"Existing Detector Ordinal Baseline (Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT)\",\n139\t    \"description\": \"将 Binoculars (Hans et al., ICML 2024) 和 Fast-DetectGPT (Bao et al., 2024) 的 连续分数校准为 ordinal depth bins。在 3×3 benchmark 数据上跑推理，optimal threshold  search 做 4-class assignment。评估 d0/d1/d2/d3 区分能力。\\n\",\n140\t    \"results\": {\n141\t      \"binoculars\": {\n142\t        \"ordinal_4class_acc\": 0.35,\n143\t        \"ordinal_4class_ci\": [\n144\t          0.32,\n145\t          0.38\n146\t        ],\n147\t        \"binary_d0v1_auc\": 0.96,\n148\t        \"ordinal_d1v2_auc\": 0.56,\n149\t        \"ordinal_d2v3_auc\": 0.53,\n150\t        \"per_class_recall\": {\n151\t          \"d0\": 0.85,\n152\t          \"d1\": 0.25,\n153\t          \"d2\": 0.15,\n154\t          \"d3\": 0.18\n155\t        },\n156\t        \"per_class_f1\": {\n157\t          \"d0\": 0.62,\n158\t          \"d1\": 0.22,\n159\t          \"d2\": 0.14,\n160\t          \"d3\": 0.17\n161\t        },\n162\t        \"confusion_pattern\": \"d1/d2/d3 heavily confused; most non-d0 samples assigned to d1 or d3 bins\"\n163\t      },\n164\t      \"fast_detectgpt\": {\n165\t        \"ordinal_4class_acc\": 0.31,\n166\t        \"ordinal_4class_ci\": [\n167\t          0.28,\n168\t          0.34\n169\t        ],\n170\t        \"binary_d0v1_auc\": 0.93,\n171\t        \"ordinal_d1v2_auc\": 0.54,\n172\t        \"ordinal_d2v3_auc\": 0.52,\n173\t        \"per_class_recall\": {\n174\t          \"d0\": 0.82,\n175\t          \"d1\": 0.2,\n176\t          \"d2\": 0.12,\n177\t          \"d3\": 0.15\n178\t        },\n179\t        \"per_class_f1\": {\n180\t          \"d0\": 0.58,\n181\t          \"d1\": 0.18,\n182\t          \"d2\": 0.11,\n183\t          \"d3\": 0.14\n184\t        },\n185\t        \"confusion_pattern\": \"even worse d2 discrimination; curvature metric saturates for synthetic→deeper-synthetic\"\n186\t      },\n187\t      \"our_rf_reference\": {\n188\t        \"4class_acc\": 0.783,\n189\t        \"gap_vs_binoculars_pp\": 43.3,\n190\t        \"gap_vs_fdgpt_pp\": 47.3\n191\t      },\n192\t      \"existing_detector_ordinal_acc_range\": [\n193\t        0.31,\n194\t        0.35\n195\t      ]\n196\t    },\n197\t    \"tables\": [\n198\t      \"Table 3: Existing detector ordinal performance vs our methods — Binoculars, Fast-DetectGPT, RF, CORAL, DivEye\",\n199\t      \"Table S3: Per-class recall/F1 for all methods, highlighting d2 as universal hardest class\"\n200\t    ],\n201\t    \"figures\": [],\n202\t    \"analysis\": \"Dream 三档一致指出的 #1 缺口，现已填补。Binoculars/FDGPT ordinal ≤35% vs RF 78.3%  形成论文中最有力的对比数据点。直接验证核心前提：ordinal depth 是新任务，需要新方法。 同时加强 \\\"no novel method\\\" 防线——贡献不是 RF（分类器选择），而是 19 维特征空间 +  task formalization 使 ordinal discrimination 成为可能，而既有工具完全做不到。 论文措辞：\\\"State-of-the-art binary detectors achieve only 31-35% ordinal accuracy,  confirming that depth estimation requires the multi-dimensional feature space we propose.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBinoculars 计算双模型 perplexity 比值（observer/performer），Fast-DetectGPT 计算条件概率 曲率（扰动法）。两者都是为 binary real-vs-synthetic 边界设计的，在 d0v1 上表现优秀 (AUC >0.93) 因为 human-vs-machine gap 正是其目标信号。\\n但 d1→d2→d3 的渐进退化涉及远更微妙的分布偏移，单一标量分数无法解析： (a) 一维分数将多维 depth degradation trajectory 压缩到一个轴上，丢失了 19 维特征空间中 编码的 ordinal 信息； (b) Binoculars 的 perplexity 比值捕获平均质量下降，但无法区分 tail-specific erosion  （p90_ppl 差异），而这正是 d1 vs d2 的核心区分信号； (c) Fast-DetectGPT 的曲率度量对 human→synthetic 的尖锐转变敏感，但对 synthetic→deeper-synthetic  饱和（曲率变化在 d1 之后趋于平缓）。\\nd1/d2/d3 的分数分布严重重叠（预计相邻 depth 的 Kolmogorov-Smirnov D ≈ 0.08-0.12）， 使得 threshold-based ordinal assignment 对非 d0 类近似随机。\\n最终 4-class accuracy：d0 被良好分离 (~85%/82% recall) 贡献 ~21%/20.5% 整体 accuracy， d1/d2/d3 各 ~20%/15%/18% recall 贡献 ~15%/10%/13%。加权后 Binoculars ~35%, FDGPT ~31%。\\nBinoculars 略优于 FDGPT (~4pp) 因为其双模型设计对渐进质量退化有略好的敏感度， 但两者都远低于 RF 78.3% (差距 43-47pp)，确认 ordinal depth estimation 是全新能力， 不可通过复用 binary detector 实现。\\n\"\n203\t  },\n204\t  {\n205\t    \"name\": \"Table 1 Bootstrap CIs\",\n206\t    \"description\": \"对 3×3 矩阵所有 9 cells 计算 bootstrap 95% CI。1000 次 bootstrap resampling from  5-fold CV results。报告 CI width 和排名稳定性分析。\\n\",\n207\t    \"results\": {\n208\t      \"mean_ci_width_pp\": 2.8,\n209\t      \"max_ci_width_pp\": 3.5,\n210\t      \"min_ci_width_pp\": 2.0,\n211\t      \"all_above_chance_25pct\": true,\n212\t      \"per_cell_bootstrap_ci\": {\n213\t        \"pythia_nucleus\": [\n214\t          0.77,\n215\t          0.794\n216\t        ],\n217\t        \"pythia_temp09\": [\n218\t          0.749,\n219\t          0.776\n220\t        ],\n221\t        \"pythia_topk50\": [\n222\t          0.683,\n223\t          0.71\n224\t        ],\n225\t        \"olmo_nucleus\": [\n226\t          0.777,\n227\t          0.803\n228\t        ],\n229\t        \"olmo_temp09\": [\n230\t          0.811,\n231\t          0.84\n232\t        ],\n233\t        \"olmo_topk50\": [\n234\t          0.729,\n235\t          0.756\n236\t        ],\n237\t        \"gpt2xl_nucleus\": [\n238\t          0.824,\n239\t          0.853\n240\t        ],\n241\t        \"gpt2xl_temp09\": [\n242\t          0.843,\n243\t          0.866\n244\t        ],\n245\t        \"gpt2xl_topk50\": [\n246\t          0.745,\n247\t          0.777\n248\t        ]\n249\t      },\n250\t      \"strategy_ranking_preserved\": true,\n251\t      \"model_ranking_preserved\": true,\n252\t      \"weakest_gap_nucleus_vs_temp09_pythia_pp\": 1.4,\n253\t      \"note\": \"nucleus-temp09 gap for Pythia is smallest (1.4pp) but both CIs non-overlapping\"\n254\t    },\n255\t    \"tables\": [\n256\t      \"Table 1 (updated): 3×3 accuracy matrix with bootstrap 95% CI in brackets\"\n257\t    ],\n258\t    \"figures\": [],\n259\t    \"analysis\": \"Dream requirement + 标准 reviewer 期望。Tight CIs (2-3pp) 确认模型间、策略间、方法间的 accuracy 差异是统计显著的。论文可以做带统计 backing 的排名声明 (\\\"GPT-2 XL consistently  achieves the highest accuracy across all strategies\\\")。Bootstrap CIs 也使 d0 confound  分析更可信——3-class CIs 同样 tight。\\n\\n\\n每 cell ~20,000 样本、5-fold CV，采样分布近似正态 (CLT)。已有 fold 级标准差 ~1-2pp （如 Pythia nucleus fold accs: 0.77-0.79），bootstrap 95% CI 对应 ~±1.5pp。 CI width 主要由 fold 间自然方差决定，而非样本量不足。\\n所有 9 cells 高于 chance 20+ pp，无 CI 接近 25% chance line。策略排名 (temp09 ≥  nucleus > topk50) 在 CI 内保持，因为策略间效应量 (~5-8pp) 显著大于 CI width (~3pp)。 模型排名 (GPT-2 XL > OLMo ≥ Pythia) 同样稳定，GPT-2 XL 领先 4-7pp。\\n唯一潜在 overlap：Pythia 的 nucleus vs temp09（差距最小 ~1.4pp），但由于 CI width ~2.5pp， 两个 CI 的上下边界仍不重叠（nucleus upper 0.794 vs temp09 lower 0.749 有间距）， 所以排名仍然稳定。这是微妙差异，不影响主叙事。\\n\"\n260\t  },\n261\t  {\n262\t    \"name\": \"Theoretical Analysis: EDD Bound + Tail Erosion Mechanism\",\n263\t    \"description\": \"Theory section 连接 depth signal 到 model collapse 理论。三个组件： (1) 从 Dohmatob (2024) contraction rates 推导 EDD 上界； (2) 从 Shumailov (2024) tail erosion 解释 p90_ppl/var_surprisal 主导地位； (3) 从 logit scaling analysis 推导 temperature 加速收敛机制。 产出：Theory section 草稿（~1 page），含 Proposition + 实验验证。\\n\",\n264\t    \"results\": {\n265\t      \"edd_bound\": {\n266\t        \"formula\": \"EDD ≤ ⌈log(ε) / log(γ)⌉ where γ = contraction rate, ε = KL threshold for AUC=0.75\",\n267\t        \"contraction_rate_estimate\": 0.75,\n268\t        \"contraction_rate_source\": \"finetune loss trajectory ratios (Pythia: 2.22→1.37→1.01, ratio ~0.73-0.74)\",\n269\t        \"kl_threshold_epsilon\": 0.04,\n270\t        \"predicted_edd_bound\": 5,\n271\t        \"empirical_edd\": 4,\n272\t        \"bound_vs_empirical_error\": 1,\n273\t        \"interpretation\": \"Bound is 5, empirical is 4. Gap=1 reflects RF operating below information-theoretic limit (~80% efficiency on 19 features). Bound is tight enough to be informative.\"\n274\t      },\n275\t      \"tail_erosion\": {\n276\t        \"mechanism\": \"Recursive fine-tuning on finite model-generated samples systematically under-represents low-probability events. Each step shrinks the tail of the token probability distribution.\",\n277\t        \"p90_ppl_prediction\": \"Monotonically decreasing with depth\",\n278\t        \"p90_ppl_empirical\": \"Confirmed: Spearman ρ = -0.82 to -0.89 across 9 cells\",\n279\t        \"var_surprisal_prediction\": \"Decreasing as distribution concentrates toward mode\",\n280\t        \"var_surprisal_empirical\": \"Confirmed: 7/9 cells var_surprisal in top-2\",\n281\t        \"quantitative_prediction\": \"p90_ppl ratio between consecutive depths ≈ γ^α where α depends on tail index, predicting ~25-35% drop d0→d1 and ~15-20% drop per subsequent step\"\n282\t      },\n283\t      \"temperature_convergence\": {\n284\t        \"mechanism\": \"Temperature τ<1 modifies logits as z/τ, uniformly rescaling all logit differences. Unlike nucleus (truncation) or top-k (removal), temperature preserves full support but amplifies high-probability tokens, accelerating convergence to attractor.\",\n285\t        \"prediction\": \"γ_temp < γ_nucleus < γ_topk (temp converges fastest, topk slowest)\",\n286\t        \"empirical_support\": \"temp09 d1 features ≈ nucleus/topk50 d2 features (GPT-2 XL temp09 d1 p90_ppl median=92.2 falls in nucleus d2 range 65-92)\",\n287\t        \"d1v2_reversal_explained\": \"Cross-strategy d1v2 AUC inversion (0.13, 0.25) follows directly: temp09 d1 has already reached the feature space that nucleus/topk50 reach at d2\"\n288\t      },\n289\t      \"feature_ranking_theory_vs_empirical\": {\n290\t        \"theoretical\": [\n291\t          \"p90_ppl\",\n292\t          \"var_surprisal\",\n293\t          \"mean_ppl\"\n294\t        ],\n295\t        \"empirical\": [\n296\t          \"p90_ppl\",\n297\t          \"var_surprisal\",\n298\t          \"p75_ppl\"\n299\t        ],\n300\t        \"agreement\": \"Top-2 exact match; top-3 partial (mean_ppl vs p75_ppl — both perplexity family)\"\n301\t      }\n302\t    },\n303\t    \"tables\": [\n304\t      \"Table 4: Theoretical EDD bound vs empirical EDD — 3 models × 2 scales, with contraction rate estimates\",\n305\t      \"Table S4: Finetune loss trajectories and derived contraction rates per model\"\n306\t    ],\n307\t    \"figures\": [],\n308\t    \"analysis\": \"Theory section 是 Dream 3.0→4.0 的关键升级。解决 \\\"no algorithmic contribution\\\" concern： (a) 可证伪预测 (EDD bound ≤5 vs empirical 4, error=1); (b) 特征主导地位的因果解释 (tail erosion → p90_ppl); (c) temperature 轨迹反转的机制解释 (logit scaling → accelerated convergence)。 将 Atlas 从 \\\"经验观察\\\" 升级为 \\\"theory-grounded characterization\\\"。\\nBound 推导不是新定理，而是将已有收敛结果 novel application 到 depth estimation setting—— 对经验论文+理论 grounding 的定位完全合适。收缩率 γ≈0.75 可从 finetune loss 数据独立验证， 使 theory section 自洽可查。\\n对应 what_if theory_section——两者是同一工作的不同描述。\\n\\n\\nDohmatob (2024) 证明了迭代重训练的模型分布以几何速率收敛到不动点（attractor 分布）， 收缩率 γ<1 取决于 synthetic-to-real 数据比例和模型逼近能力。在我们的全合成递归链设定中， γ 由模型完美复制自身输出分布的能力决定。\\n从经验 finetune loss 轨迹估计 γ：Pythia d0 loss 2.22 → d1 1.37（比率 0.617）→ d2 1.01 （比率 0.737）。取 d1→d2 比率（更稳定，排除 d0→d1 的大跳变）得 γ ≈ 0.75。 GPT-2 XL: 2.55→1.715→1.342，比率 0.783→0.782。OLMo: 2.27→1.65→1.23，比率 0.727→0.745。 三模型均值 γ ≈ 0.75，一致性高。\\nEDD bound 推导：每步 KL divergence 以 γ 衰减。AUC=0.75 阈值对应 KL ≈ ε（从 d0v1  数据点标定 AUC-KL 映射，d0v1 AUC=0.99 对应 KL≈0.5，线性插值到 AUC=0.75 得 ε≈0.04）。 Bound = ⌈log(0.04)/log(0.75)⌉ = ⌈11.2⌉ = 12 是信息论上限。RF on 19 features 的实际效率 ~35-40%（特征不完整 + 分类器非最优），effective bound ≈ 12 × 0.4 ≈ 5。 Empirical EDD=4，误差 1，在预期范围内。Bound 足够 tight 以具有信息量（排除 EDD=10 等假设）， 但不过度 tight 以避免被实验数据精确反驳。\\nTail erosion 连接直接而因果：Shumailov 2024 证明递归训练首先侵蚀低概率事件（分布 \\\"tail\\\"）。 p90_ppl 是 tail 的直接度量——第 90 百分位 per-token perplexity 反映最 \\\"surprising\\\" 的 tokens。 随着 tail 被侵蚀，p90_ppl 单调下降。var_surprisal 捕获 surprisal 分布的整体展宽度， 随分布向 mode 集中而收窄。理论预测 top-2 = {p90_ppl, var_surprisal}，实验完美验证。\\nTemperature 加速收敛：logit z/τ 的均匀缩放保持了完整支撑（不截断）但放大了高概率 token  的相对权重，每步将更多概率质量 shift 向 mode，加速分布集中。与 nucleus（截断低概率 token， 保留剩余分布形状）和 top-k（直接移除 tail，但剩余分布相对稳定）相比，temperature  在每步产生最大的分布中心化效应。量化预测 temp09 d1 ≈ nucleus d2 特征位置， 已由 GPT-2 XL 数据精确确认 (temp09 d1 p90_ppl median=92.2 in nucleus d2 range 65-92)。\\n\"\n309\t  },\n310\t  {\n311\t    \"name\": \"API Model Recursive Chains\",\n312\t    \"description\": \"两条路径验证 API 模型 depth signal: (a) GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API 递归 d0-d3 链  (需 OpenAI key)。(b) Prompted recursive chain (rewrite/continue prompts，无 fine-tune)。 19 特征提取 + RF 分类。\\n\",\n313\t    \"results\": {\n314\t      \"finetuned_chain\": {\n315\t        \"rf_4class_acc\": 0.68,\n316\t        \"rf_4class_ci\": [\n317\t          0.66,\n318\t          0.7\n319\t        ],\n320\t        \"lr_4class_acc\": 0.62,\n321\t        \"d0v1_auc\": 0.97,\n322\t        \"d1v2_auc\": 0.78,\n323\t        \"d2v3_auc\": 0.68,\n324\t        \"top_features\": [\n325\t          \"p90_ppl\",\n326\t          \"var_surprisal\",\n327\t          \"mean_ppl\",\n328\t          \"p75_ppl\",\n329\t          \"mean_surprisal\"\n330\t        ],\n331\t        \"feature_overlap_with_local_top2\": 2,\n332\t        \"per_class_recall\": {\n333\t          \"d0\": 0.95,\n334\t          \"d1\": 0.72,\n335\t          \"d2\": 0.44,\n336\t          \"d3\": 0.62\n337\t        }\n338\t      },\n339\t      \"prompted_chain\": {\n340\t        \"rf_4class_acc\": 0.55,\n341\t        \"rf_4class_ci\": [\n342\t          0.53,\n343\t          0.57\n344\t        ],\n345\t        \"lr_4class_acc\": 0.48,\n346\t        \"d0v1_auc\": 0.89,\n347\t        \"d1v2_auc\": 0.62,\n348\t        \"d2v3_auc\": 0.55,\n349\t        \"top_features\": [\n350\t          \"p90_ppl\",\n351\t          \"var_surprisal\",\n352\t          \"mean_surprisal\",\n353\t          \"p75_ppl\",\n354\t          \"prob_std\"\n355\t        ],\n356\t        \"per_class_recall\": {\n357\t          \"d0\": 0.88,\n358\t          \"d1\": 0.52,\n359\t          \"d2\": 0.28,\n360\t          \"d3\": 0.48\n361\t        }\n362\t      },\n363\t      \"reference_points\": {\n364\t        \"local_1b_mean\": 0.783,\n365\t        \"instruct_model\": 0.474,\n366\t        \"prompted_gen\": 0.695,\n367\t        \"chance\": 0.25\n368\t      }\n369\t    },\n370\t    \"tables\": [\n371\t      \"Table S6: API model depth estimation — fine-tuned vs prompted vs local baselines, with per-class recall\"\n372\t    ],\n373\t    \"figures\": [],\n374\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix 补充实验但 ecological validity 价值高。Fine-tuned chain 确认 depth signal  在商用模型中存在。Prompted chain 建立下界。合并 instruct (47.4%) + prompted gen (69.5%) +  API fine-tune (68%) + prompted chain (55%)，完整图景：\\\"depth signal is a general property  of recursive text generation, present across local fine-tuning, API fine-tuning, and  prompted rewriting chains, with magnitude proportional to the degree of distribution shift.\\\"\\n对 best tier 整体叙事的贡献：扩展 \\\"feasible and robust\\\" claim 到 API setting， 虽然是 Appendix 级别但消除 \\\"only works with local fine-tuning\\\" 的潜在质疑。\\n\\n\\nFine-tuned API chain: GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning 创建真实递归分布偏移（每个 depth 的模型 从前一 depth 的输出学习），机制类似于本地 LoRA fine-tuning。但 API fine-tuning 有约束： epoch 数有限、超参控制受限、可能有 safety guardrail 残余。68% accuracy 介于本地 1B (78%)  和 instruct model (47.4%) 之间，反映 API fine-tuning 的混合性质（继承 RLHF 正则化 但仍发生真实分布偏移）。d2 recall 最低 (0.44) 延续 1B 模式。\\nFeature universality 部分保持：p90_ppl + var_surprisal 仍在 top-2，因为 tail erosion  机制与 API vs local 无关——来自有限样本 fine-tuning 的分布尾部侵蚀是通用的。 但整体信号强度衰减 ~10pp，反映 API 模型的 RLHF 残余正则化效应。\\nPrompted chain: 不 fine-tune 意味着每个 \\\"depth\\\" 只是同一模型对前一输出的条件生成。 不会替换模型分布——depth signal 来自累积的风格漂移（更通用、多样性更低、重复更多）， 但效应远弱于 fine-tuning-based chains。55% accuracy 仍然显著高于 chance (25%)， 建立了 \\\"最弱迁移设定\\\" 的下界。d2 recall 仅 28% 因为 prompted rewriting 在 d2  的分布偏移已经非常微弱。\\n与 instruct model (47.4%) 的关系：instruct model 是基于 fine-tuning 但有强 RLHF， API fine-tuned chain 68% > instruct 47.4% 因为递归 fine-tuning 积累的偏移大于  单次 RLHF 的正则化效应。Prompted chain 55% > instruct 47.4% 可能因为 GPT-4o-mini  基础模型更强，但差距不大。\\n\"\n375\t  },\n376\t  {\n377\t    \"name\": \"DCOL Component Ablation\",\n378\t    \"description\": \"DCOL loss 组件消融。已取消——DCOL v6 (RoBERTa-large) 失败，前置条件 plan_004 不满足。\",\n379\t    \"results\": {\n380\t      \"status\": \"cancelled\",\n381\t      \"reason\": \"DCOL v1-v6 全部失败 (embedding collapse / OOM / catastrophic forgetting / NaN / severe overfitting)。无消融目标。\"\n382\t    },\n383\t    \"tables\": [],\n384\t    \"figures\": [],\n385\t    \"analysis\": \"N/A — experiment cancelled. DCOL failure documented in negative analysis section (Section 6.3).\\n\\nDCOL 在 6 次尝试中结构性失败：contrastive ordinal learning 在文本 depth estimation 上 缺乏将相邻 depth 分离到 embedding space 的归纳偏置。v6 (RoBERTa-large) 最稳定但仍严重 过拟合 (train 75% vs val 64.4%)，低于 RF baseline 13.7pp。失败被记录为 negative finding： \\\"Contrastive ordinal learning's inherent limitations for text depth estimation\\\"。 论文 framing 为 \\\"task formalization + systematic empirical study\\\"（非 method paper）， DCOL 失败不削弱贡献——反而支持 \\\"19 维统计特征是该问题正确抽象层级\\\" 的论点。\\n\"\n386\t  }\n387\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"293a4726-1263-4b10-8462-4c709e6f178f","uuid":"59fec0b0-f350-4c61-b351-b5a6a9a07a1a","timestamp":"2026-05-18T16:23:49.836Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_2/projects/recursive_gen_depth_est/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T160031/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"14B Clean FP16 Scale Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-14B FP16 (无量化) on 96GB RTX PRO 6000。Nucleus p=0.95，d0-d3 递归 LoRA  fine-tuning 链。Pythia-1.4B reference model 提取 19 维统计特征。RF/LR 5-fold CV。 Binary pairwise d0-d5 确定 EDD。验证 depth signal 在 14B 规模是否持续。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rf_4class_acc\": 0.76,\n      \"rf_4class_ci\": [\n        0.745,\n        0.775\n      ],\n      \"lr_4class_acc\": 0.72,\n      \"lr_4class_ci\": [\n        0.705,\n        0.735\n      ],\n      \"rf_3class_acc\": 0.71,\n      \"rf_3class_ci\": [\n        0.692,\n        0.728\n      ],\n      \"pairwise_auc_rf\": {\n        \"d0v1\": 0.988,\n        \"d0v2\": 0.997,\n        \"d0v3\": 0.999,\n        \"d1v2\": 0.87,\n        \"d1v3\": 0.975,\n        \"d2v3\": 0.79\n      },\n      \"per_class_recall\": {\n        \"d0\": 0.97,\n        \"d1\": 0.82,\n        \"d2\": 0.58,\n        \"d3\": 0.72\n      },\n      \"per_class_f1\": {\n        \"d0\": 0.96,\n        \"d1\": 0.81,\n        \"d2\": 0.6,\n        \"d3\": 0.7\n      },\n      \"top_features\": [\n        \"p90_ppl (0.19)\",\n        \"var_surprisal (0.16)\",\n        \"p75_ppl (0.11)\",\n        \"mean_surprisal (0.09)\",\n        \"mean_ppl (0.07)\"\n      ],\n      \"feature_overlap_with_1b_top2\": 2,\n      \"finetune_losses\": {\n        \"depth_0\": 1.95,\n        \"depth_1\": 1.25,\n        \"depth_2\": 0.92\n      },\n      \"binary_pairwise_auc\": {\n        \"d1v2\": 0.93,\n        \"d2v3\": 0.86,\n        \"d3v4\": 0.76,\n        \"d4v5\": 0.69\n      },\n      \"edd_at_075\": 4,\n      \"code_contamination_narrow_max\": 0.02\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: Scale validation — Qwen2.5-14B row alongside 3×1B models (4-class acc, d1v2 AUC, EDD)\",\n      \"Table S2: 14B per-class precision/recall/F1 + binary pairwise AUC for EDD determination\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"14B 结果直接启用 Claim 1 中 \\\"1B-14B scale robustness\\\" 子句。76% 是 chance (25%) 的 3 倍， 确认 ordinal depth signal 在主流模型规模持续存在且无需量化（消除 7B QLoRA 矛盾结果的干扰）。 Feature universality 现在覆盖 4 个模型家族、10+ settings——论文最强实证发现。 EDD=4 跨尺度一致性将 Atlas 从 \\\"1B-only observation\\\" 升级为 \\\"scale-invariant structural  property of recursive generation\\\"。~4pp 下降是预期中的且可解释（larger model, slower collapse）， 不是弱点而是支撑 tail erosion 理论的额外证据。\\n\\n\\n14B 模型容量 ~10x 于 1B，每步递归 fine-tuning 产生的分布偏移更小（更强的模型更接近地复制训练数据）， 导致 per-step 特征差异压缩。这解释了 ~4pp 的准确率下降（76% vs 1B nucleus 均值 80.1%）。\\n但 tail erosion 机制 (Shumailov 2024) 是 scale-invariant 的：递归训练在有限样本上系统性地 under-represent 低概率事件，与模型大小无关。因为采样过程本身截断了真实分布的尾部——无论模型多大， 从有限样本 fine-tune 都会丢失 tail events。p90_ppl 直接度量这种 tail contraction（每步递归 第 90 百分位 per-token perplexity 下降），var_surprisal 捕获 surprisal 分布随分布集中向 mode  的收窄。两者在 14B 仍然 top-2/3 是因为度量的是文本分布属性而非模型架构属性。\\nEDD=4 匹配 1B 是因为：更大模型的更慢收缩率被 reference model (Pythia-1.4B) 对更精细分布差异的 同样降低的敏感度所抵消——14B d3 和 d4 的差异更微妙，但 Pythia 对 14B 生成文本的基线敏感度也更低 （domain shift），两个效应大致相消，使得 AUC=0.75 阈值在同一相对位置（depth 4）被达到。\\nd3v4 AUC 0.76（刚过阈值）反映 depth 4 的信号仍可检测但微弱；d4v5 0.69 跌破阈值，符合几何收敛 到 attractor 的预期。d2 recall 最低 (0.58) 与 1B 模式一致——d2 被夹在 d1 和 d3 之间， 是最难区分的 depth class。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Wild-data Calibration (C4/FineWeb/RedPajama)\",\n    \"description\": \"系统化 wild-data 评估。用 Pythia/OLMo/GPT-2 XL 三个 reference model 分别提取 19 特征， 在 C4、FineWeb、RedPajama 各 10K passages 上用 3×3 训练好的 RF 分类器做 depth 预测。 分析 depth 分布、FPR 模式、跨 reference model 一致性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"c4\": {\n        \"n_passages\": 10000,\n        \"d0_pct_mean\": 72.0,\n        \"d0_pct_range_across_ref\": [\n          66.0,\n          95.3\n        ],\n        \"d1_pct_mean\": 22.0,\n        \"d2_pct_mean\": 3.5,\n        \"d3_pct_mean\": 2.5,\n        \"fpr_mean\": 28.0,\n        \"fpr_range_across_ref\": [\n          4.7,\n          34.0\n        ],\n        \"cross_model_d0_agreement_pct\": 88\n      },\n      \"fineweb\": {\n        \"n_passages\": 10000,\n        \"d0_pct_mean\": 82.0,\n        \"d0_pct_range_across_ref\": [\n          78.0,\n          88.0\n        ],\n        \"d1_pct_mean\": 15.5,\n        \"d2_pct_mean\": 1.5,\n        \"d3_pct_mean\": 1.0,\n        \"fpr_mean\": 18.0,\n        \"fpr_range_across_ref\": [\n          12.0,\n          22.0\n        ],\n        \"cross_model_d0_agreement_pct\": 91\n      },\n      \"redpajama\": {\n        \"n_passages\": 10000,\n        \"d0_pct_mean\": 81.0,\n        \"d0_pct_range_across_ref\": [\n          76.0,\n          90.0\n        ],\n        \"d1_pct_mean\": 15.0,\n        \"d2_pct_mean\": 2.5,\n        \"d3_pct_mean\": 1.5,\n        \"fpr_mean\": 19.0,\n        \"fpr_range_across_ref\": [\n          10.0,\n          24.0\n        ],\n        \"cross_model_d0_agreement_pct\": 89\n      },\n      \"editorial_text_fpr\": \"<3%\",\n      \"template_content_fpr\": \"35-50%\",\n      \"cross_model_rank_corr_d0_pct\": 0.82,\n      \"olmo_systematic_lowest_fpr\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: Wild-data depth distributions — corpus × reference model (3×3 grid)\",\n      \"Table S5: FPR breakdown by content type (editorial vs template vs SEO), with examples\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Wild-data calibration 弥合 controlled→ecological validity 的最后一步。分类器在真实语料上 行为连贯：高质量文本→d0，template 内容→d1，无虚假 d2/d3。支撑 Discussion 中  \\\"depth-graduated curation\\\" 论点。论文表述：\\\"our classifier exhibits meaningful behavior on  uncurated web text, correctly separating editorial from template-generated content, though  definitive depth labels are unavailable for wild data.\\\"\\n\\n\\n已有 wild-data 实验已建立核心模式：编辑质量高的文本 (WikiText, OpenWebText) FPR <3%， web-crawl (C4, FineWeb) FPR 15-34%。三模型系统化分析确认这不是单一 reference model 的 artifact。\\nFPR 差异的根因已确认：web-crawl 语料中 15-30% 是 template/SEO/机器翻译内容，这些文本与 模型生成文本共享统计指纹（高重复率、压缩的 perplexity tail、低词汇多样性）。这不是真正的  false positive——分类器正确识别了具有 \\\"shallow synthetic\\\" 特征的文本。\\nOLMo 系统性 FPR 最低（已确认：C4 4.72% vs Pythia 20.2%/GPT-2 XL 22.4%），因为 OLMo  d1-d3 特征与 d0 的差异更大，产生更宽的 d0 决策边界。GPT-2 XL FPR 最高因为信号最强—— d0 和 d1 的 feature gap 更小，导致 template 内容更容易落入 d1 范围。\\nCross-model d0 agreement ~88-91% 意味着三个 reference model 对同一段 passage 的 d0/non-d0 判断高度一致，确认信号在文本本身而非 reference model 的偏差。d1-heavy 分布（vs d2/d3 近零） 符合预期：大多数 \\\"synthetic-looking\\\" web 文本类似浅层模型输出，不是深度递归文本。\\nFineWeb 和 RedPajama 的 FPR 低于 C4 反映了各自的质量过滤：FineWeb 有激进的去重和质量过滤， RedPajama 混合了 Wikipedia/books/ArXiv 等高质量源。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Existing Detector Ordinal Baseline (Binoculars + Fast-DetectGPT)\",\n    \"description\": \"将 Binoculars (Hans et al., ICML 2024) 和 Fast-DetectGPT (Bao et al., 2024) 的 连续分数校准为 ordinal depth bins。在 3×3 benchmark 数据上跑推理，optimal threshold  search 做 4-class assignment。评估 d0/d1/d2/d3 区分能力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"binoculars\": {\n        \"ordinal_4class_acc\": 0.35,\n        \"ordinal_4class_ci\": [\n          0.32,\n          0.38\n        ],\n        \"binary_d0v1_auc\": 0.96,\n        \"ordinal_d1v2_auc\": 0.56,\n        \"ordinal_d2v3_auc\": 0.53,\n        \"per_class_recall\": {\n          \"d0\": 0.85,\n          \"d1\": 0.25,\n          \"d2\": 0.15,\n          \"d3\": 0.18\n        },\n        \"per_class_f1\": {\n          \"d0\": 0.62,\n          \"d1\": 0.22,\n          \"d2\": 0.14,\n          \"d3\": 0.17\n        },\n        \"confusion_pattern\": \"d1/d2/d3 heavily confused; most non-d0 samples assigned to d1 or d3 bins\"\n      },\n      \"fast_detectgpt\": {\n        \"ordinal_4class_acc\": 0.31,\n        \"ordinal_4class_ci\": [\n          0.28,\n          0.34\n        ],\n        \"binary_d0v1_auc\": 0.93,\n        \"ordinal_d1v2_auc\": 0.54,\n        \"ordinal_d2v3_auc\": 0.52,\n        \"per_class_recall\": {\n          \"d0\": 0.82,\n          \"d1\": 0.2,\n          \"d2\": 0.12,\n          \"d3\": 0.15\n        },\n        \"per_class_f1\": {\n          \"d0\": 0.58,\n          \"d1\": 0.18,\n          \"d2\": 0.11,\n          \"d3\": 0.14\n        },\n        \"confusion_pattern\": \"even worse d2 discrimination; curvature metric saturates for synthetic→deeper-synthetic\"\n      },\n      \"our_rf_reference\": {\n        \"4class_acc\": 0.783,\n        \"gap_vs_binoculars_pp\": 43.3,\n        \"gap_vs_fdgpt_pp\": 47.3\n      },\n      \"existing_detector_ordinal_acc_range\": [\n        0.31,\n        0.35\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3: Existing detector ordinal performance vs our methods — Binoculars, Fast-DetectGPT, RF, CORAL, DivEye\",\n      \"Table S3: Per-class recall/F1 for all methods, highlighting d2 as universal hardest class\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Dream 三档一致指出的 #1 缺口，现已填补。Binoculars/FDGPT ordinal ≤35% vs RF 78.3%  形成论文中最有力的对比数据点。直接验证核心前提：ordinal depth 是新任务，需要新方法。 同时加强 \\\"no novel method\\\" 防线——贡献不是 RF（分类器选择），而是 19 维特征空间 +  task formalization 使 ordinal discrimination 成为可能，而既有工具完全做不到。 论文措辞：\\\"State-of-the-art binary detectors achieve only 31-35% ordinal accuracy,  confirming that depth estimation requires the multi-dimensional feature space we propose.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBinoculars 计算双模型 perplexity 比值（observer/performer），Fast-DetectGPT 计算条件概率 曲率（扰动法）。两者都是为 binary real-vs-synthetic 边界设计的，在 d0v1 上表现优秀 (AUC >0.93) 因为 human-vs-machine gap 正是其目标信号。\\n但 d1→d2→d3 的渐进退化涉及远更微妙的分布偏移，单一标量分数无法解析： (a) 一维分数将多维 depth degradation trajectory 压缩到一个轴上，丢失了 19 维特征空间中 编码的 ordinal 信息； (b) Binoculars 的 perplexity 比值捕获平均质量下降，但无法区分 tail-specific erosion  （p90_ppl 差异），而这正是 d1 vs d2 的核心区分信号； (c) Fast-DetectGPT 的曲率度量对 human→synthetic 的尖锐转变敏感，但对 synthetic→deeper-synthetic  饱和（曲率变化在 d1 之后趋于平缓）。\\nd1/d2/d3 的分数分布严重重叠（预计相邻 depth 的 Kolmogorov-Smirnov D ≈ 0.08-0.12）， 使得 threshold-based ordinal assignment 对非 d0 类近似随机。\\n最终 4-class accuracy：d0 被良好分离 (~85%/82% recall) 贡献 ~21%/20.5% 整体 accuracy， d1/d2/d3 各 ~20%/15%/18% recall 贡献 ~15%/10%/13%。加权后 Binoculars ~35%, FDGPT ~31%。\\nBinoculars 略优于 FDGPT (~4pp) 因为其双模型设计对渐进质量退化有略好的敏感度， 但两者都远低于 RF 78.3% (差距 43-47pp)，确认 ordinal depth estimation 是全新能力， 不可通过复用 binary detector 实现。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Table 1 Bootstrap CIs\",\n    \"description\": \"对 3×3 矩阵所有 9 cells 计算 bootstrap 95% CI。1000 次 bootstrap resampling from  5-fold CV results。报告 CI width 和排名稳定性分析。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mean_ci_width_pp\": 2.8,\n      \"max_ci_width_pp\": 3.5,\n      \"min_ci_width_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"all_above_chance_25pct\": true,\n      \"per_cell_bootstrap_ci\": {\n        \"pythia_nucleus\": [\n          0.77,\n          0.794\n        ],\n        \"pythia_temp09\": [\n          0.749,\n          0.776\n        ],\n        \"pythia_topk50\": [\n          0.683,\n          0.71\n        ],\n        \"olmo_nucleus\": [\n          0.777,\n          0.803\n        ],\n        \"olmo_temp09\": [\n          0.811,\n          0.84\n        ],\n        \"olmo_topk50\": [\n          0.729,\n          0.756\n        ],\n        \"gpt2xl_nucleus\": [\n          0.824,\n          0.853\n        ],\n        \"gpt2xl_temp09\": [\n          0.843,\n          0.866\n        ],\n        \"gpt2xl_topk50\": [\n          0.745,\n          0.777\n        ]\n      },\n      \"strategy_ranking_preserved\": true,\n      \"model_ranking_preserved\": true,\n      \"weakest_gap_nucleus_vs_temp09_pythia_pp\": 1.4,\n      \"note\": \"nucleus-temp09 gap for Pythia is smallest (1.4pp) but both CIs non-overlapping\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1 (updated): 3×3 accuracy matrix with bootstrap 95% CI in brackets\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Dream requirement + 标准 reviewer 期望。Tight CIs (2-3pp) 确认模型间、策略间、方法间的 accuracy 差异是统计显著的。论文可以做带统计 backing 的排名声明 (\\\"GPT-2 XL consistently  achieves the highest accuracy across all strategies\\\")。Bootstrap CIs 也使 d0 confound  分析更可信——3-class CIs 同样 tight。\\n\\n\\n每 cell ~20,000 样本、5-fold CV，采样分布近似正态 (CLT)。已有 fold 级标准差 ~1-2pp （如 Pythia nucleus fold accs: 0.77-0.79），bootstrap 95% CI 对应 ~±1.5pp。 CI width 主要由 fold 间自然方差决定，而非样本量不足。\\n所有 9 cells 高于 chance 20+ pp，无 CI 接近 25% chance line。策略排名 (temp09 ≥  nucleus > topk50) 在 CI 内保持，因为策略间效应量 (~5-8pp) 显著大于 CI width (~3pp)。 模型排名 (GPT-2 XL > OLMo ≥ Pythia) 同样稳定，GPT-2 XL 领先 4-7pp。\\n唯一潜在 overlap：Pythia 的 nucleus vs temp09（差距最小 ~1.4pp），但由于 CI width ~2.5pp， 两个 CI 的上下边界仍不重叠（nucleus upper 0.794 vs temp09 lower 0.749 有间距）， 所以排名仍然稳定。这是微妙差异，不影响主叙事。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Theoretical Analysis: EDD Bound + Tail Erosion Mechanism\",\n    \"description\": \"Theory section 连接 depth signal 到 model collapse 理论。三个组件： (1) 从 Dohmatob (2024) contraction rates 推导 EDD 上界； (2) 从 Shumailov (2024) tail erosion 解释 p90_ppl/var_surprisal 主导地位； (3) 从 logit scaling analysis 推导 temperature 加速收敛机制。 产出：Theory section 草稿（~1 page），含 Proposition + 实验验证。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"edd_bound\": {\n        \"formula\": \"EDD ≤ ⌈log(ε) / log(γ)⌉ where γ = contraction rate, ε = KL threshold for AUC=0.75\",\n        \"contraction_rate_estimate\": 0.75,\n        \"contraction_rate_source\": \"finetune loss trajectory ratios (Pythia: 2.22→1.37→1.01, ratio ~0.73-0.74)\",\n        \"kl_threshold_epsilon\": 0.04,\n        \"predicted_edd_bound\": 5,\n        \"empirical_edd\": 4,\n        \"bound_vs_empirical_error\": 1,\n        \"interpretation\": \"Bound is 5, empirical is 4. Gap=1 reflects RF operating below information-theoretic limit (~80% efficiency on 19 features). Bound is tight enough to be informative.\"\n      },\n      \"tail_erosion\": {\n        \"mechanism\": \"Recursive fine-tuning on finite model-generated samples systematically under-represents low-probability events. Each step shrinks the tail of the token probability distribution.\",\n        \"p90_ppl_prediction\": \"Monotonically decreasing with depth\",\n        \"p90_ppl_empirical\": \"Confirmed: Spearman ρ = -0.82 to -0.89 across 9 cells\",\n        \"var_surprisal_prediction\": \"Decreasing as distribution concentrates toward mode\",\n        \"var_surprisal_empirical\": \"Confirmed: 7/9 cells var_surprisal in top-2\",\n        \"quantitative_prediction\": \"p90_ppl ratio between consecutive depths ≈ γ^α where α depends on tail index, predicting ~25-35% drop d0→d1 and ~15-20% drop per subsequent step\"\n      },\n      \"temperature_convergence\": {\n        \"mechanism\": \"Temperature τ<1 modifies logits as z/τ, uniformly rescaling all logit differences. Unlike nucleus (truncation) or top-k (removal), temperature preserves full support but amplifies high-probability tokens, accelerating convergence to attractor.\",\n        \"prediction\": \"γ_temp < γ_nucleus < γ_topk (temp converges fastest, topk slowest)\",\n        \"empirical_support\": \"temp09 d1 features ≈ nucleus/topk50 d2 features (GPT-2 XL temp09 d1 p90_ppl median=92.2 falls in nucleus d2 range 65-92)\",\n        \"d1v2_reversal_explained\": \"Cross-strategy d1v2 AUC inversion (0.13, 0.25) follows directly: temp09 d1 has already reached the feature space that nucleus/topk50 reach at d2\"\n      },\n      \"feature_ranking_theory_vs_empirical\": {\n        \"theoretical\": [\n          \"p90_ppl\",\n          \"var_surprisal\",\n          \"mean_ppl\"\n        ],\n        \"empirical\": [\n          \"p90_ppl\",\n          \"var_surprisal\",\n          \"p75_ppl\"\n        ],\n        \"agreement\": \"Top-2 exact match; top-3 partial (mean_ppl vs p75_ppl — both perplexity family)\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: Theoretical EDD bound vs empirical EDD — 3 models × 2 scales, with contraction rate estimates\",\n      \"Table S4: Finetune loss trajectories and derived contraction rates per model\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Theory section 是 Dream 3.0→4.0 的关键升级。解决 \\\"no algorithmic contribution\\\" concern： (a) 可证伪预测 (EDD bound ≤5 vs empirical 4, error=1); (b) 特征主导地位的因果解释 (tail erosion → p90_ppl); (c) temperature 轨迹反转的机制解释 (logit scaling → accelerated convergence)。 将 Atlas 从 \\\"经验观察\\\" 升级为 \\\"theory-grounded characterization\\\"。\\nBound 推导不是新定理，而是将已有收敛结果 novel application 到 depth estimation setting—— 对经验论文+理论 grounding 的定位完全合适。收缩率 γ≈0.75 可从 finetune loss 数据独立验证， 使 theory section 自洽可查。\\n对应 what_if theory_section——两者是同一工作的不同描述。\\n\\n\\nDohmatob (2024) 证明了迭代重训练的模型分布以几何速率收敛到不动点（attractor 分布）， 收缩率 γ<1 取决于 synthetic-to-real 数据比例和模型逼近能力。在我们的全合成递归链设定中， γ 由模型完美复制自身输出分布的能力决定。\\n从经验 finetune loss 轨迹估计 γ：Pythia d0 loss 2.22 → d1 1.37（比率 0.617）→ d2 1.01 （比率 0.737）。取 d1→d2 比率（更稳定，排除 d0→d1 的大跳变）得 γ ≈ 0.75。 GPT-2 XL: 2.55→1.715→1.342，比率 0.783→0.782。OLMo: 2.27→1.65→1.23，比率 0.727→0.745。 三模型均值 γ ≈ 0.75，一致性高。\\nEDD bound 推导：每步 KL divergence 以 γ 衰减。AUC=0.75 阈值对应 KL ≈ ε（从 d0v1  数据点标定 AUC-KL 映射，d0v1 AUC=0.99 对应 KL≈0.5，线性插值到 AUC=0.75 得 ε≈0.04）。 Bound = ⌈log(0.04)/log(0.75)⌉ = ⌈11.2⌉ = 12 是信息论上限。RF on 19 features 的实际效率 ~35-40%（特征不完整 + 分类器非最优），effective bound ≈ 12 × 0.4 ≈ 5。 Empirical EDD=4，误差 1，在预期范围内。Bound 足够 tight 以具有信息量（排除 EDD=10 等假设）， 但不过度 tight 以避免被实验数据精确反驳。\\nTail erosion 连接直接而因果：Shumailov 2024 证明递归训练首先侵蚀低概率事件（分布 \\\"tail\\\"）。 p90_ppl 是 tail 的直接度量——第 90 百分位 per-token perplexity 反映最 \\\"surprising\\\" 的 tokens。 随着 tail 被侵蚀，p90_ppl 单调下降。var_surprisal 捕获 surprisal 分布的整体展宽度， 随分布向 mode 集中而收窄。理论预测 top-2 = {p90_ppl, var_surprisal}，实验完美验证。\\nTemperature 加速收敛：logit z/τ 的均匀缩放保持了完整支撑（不截断）但放大了高概率 token  的相对权重，每步将更多概率质量 shift 向 mode，加速分布集中。与 nucleus（截断低概率 token， 保留剩余分布形状）和 top-k（直接移除 tail，但剩余分布相对稳定）相比，temperature  在每步产生最大的分布中心化效应。量化预测 temp09 d1 ≈ nucleus d2 特征位置， 已由 GPT-2 XL 数据精确确认 (temp09 d1 p90_ppl median=92.2 in nucleus d2 range 65-92)。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"API Model Recursive Chains\",\n    \"description\": \"两条路径验证 API 模型 depth signal: (a) GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning API 递归 d0-d3 链  (需 OpenAI key)。(b) Prompted recursive chain (rewrite/continue prompts，无 fine-tune)。 19 特征提取 + RF 分类。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"finetuned_chain\": {\n        \"rf_4class_acc\": 0.68,\n        \"rf_4class_ci\": [\n          0.66,\n          0.7\n        ],\n        \"lr_4class_acc\": 0.62,\n        \"d0v1_auc\": 0.97,\n        \"d1v2_auc\": 0.78,\n        \"d2v3_auc\": 0.68,\n        \"top_features\": [\n          \"p90_ppl\",\n          \"var_surprisal\",\n          \"mean_ppl\",\n          \"p75_ppl\",\n          \"mean_surprisal\"\n        ],\n        \"feature_overlap_with_local_top2\": 2,\n        \"per_class_recall\": {\n          \"d0\": 0.95,\n          \"d1\": 0.72,\n          \"d2\": 0.44,\n          \"d3\": 0.62\n        }\n      },\n      \"prompted_chain\": {\n        \"rf_4class_acc\": 0.55,\n        \"rf_4class_ci\": [\n          0.53,\n          0.57\n        ],\n        \"lr_4class_acc\": 0.48,\n        \"d0v1_auc\": 0.89,\n        \"d1v2_auc\": 0.62,\n        \"d2v3_auc\": 0.55,\n        \"top_features\": [\n          \"p90_ppl\",\n          \"var_surprisal\",\n          \"mean_surprisal\",\n          \"p75_ppl\",\n          \"prob_std\"\n        ],\n        \"per_class_recall\": {\n          \"d0\": 0.88,\n          \"d1\": 0.52,\n          \"d2\": 0.28,\n          \"d3\": 0.48\n        }\n      },\n      \"reference_points\": {\n        \"local_1b_mean\": 0.783,\n        \"instruct_model\": 0.474,\n        \"prompted_gen\": 0.695,\n        \"chance\": 0.25\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table S6: API model depth estimation — fine-tuned vs prompted vs local baselines, with per-class recall\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix 补充实验但 ecological validity 价值高。Fine-tuned chain 确认 depth signal  在商用模型中存在。Prompted chain 建立下界。合并 instruct (47.4%) + prompted gen (69.5%) +  API fine-tune (68%) + prompted chain (55%)，完整图景：\\\"depth signal is a general property  of recursive text generation, present across local fine-tuning, API fine-tuning, and  prompted rewriting chains, with magnitude proportional to the degree of distribution shift.\\\"\\n对 best tier 整体叙事的贡献：扩展 \\\"feasible and robust\\\" claim 到 API setting， 虽然是 Appendix 级别但消除 \\\"only works with local fine-tuning\\\" 的潜在质疑。\\n\\n\\nFine-tuned API chain: GPT-4o-mini fine-tuning 创建真实递归分布偏移（每个 depth 的模型 从前一 depth 的输出学习），机制类似于本地 LoRA fine-tuning。但 API fine-tuning 有约束： epoch 数有限、超参控制受限、可能有 safety guardrail 残余。68% accuracy 介于本地 1B (78%)  和 instruct model (47.4%) 之间，反映 API fine-tuning 的混合性质（继承 RLHF 正则化 但仍发生真实分布偏移）。d2 recall 最低 (0.44) 延续 1B 模式。\\nFeature universality 部分保持：p90_ppl + var_surprisal 仍在 top-2，因为 tail erosion  机制与 API vs local 无关——来自有限样本 fine-tuning 的分布尾部侵蚀是通用的。 但整体信号强度衰减 ~10pp，反映 API 模型的 RLHF 残余正则化效应。\\nPrompted chain: 不 fine-tune 意味着每个 \\\"depth\\\" 只是同一模型对前一输出的条件生成。 不会替换模型分布——depth signal 来自累积的风格漂移（更通用、多样性更低、重复更多）， 但效应远弱于 fine-tuning-based chains。55% accuracy 仍然显著高于 chance (25%)， 建立了 \\\"最弱迁移设定\\\" 的下界。d2 recall 仅 28% 因为 prompted rewriting 在 d2  的分布偏移已经非常微弱。\\n与 instruct model (47.4%) 的关系：instruct model 是基于 fine-tuning 但有强 RLHF， API fine-tuned chain 68% > instruct 47.4% 因为递归 fine-tuning 积累的偏移大于  单次 RLHF 的正则化效应。Prompted chain 55% > instruct 47.4% 可能因为 GPT-4o-mini  基础模型更强，但差距不大。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DCOL Component Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"DCOL loss 组件消融。已取消——DCOL v6 (RoBERTa-large) 失败，前置条件 plan_004 不满足。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"cancelled\",\n      \"reason\": \"DCOL v1-v6 全部失败 (embedding collapse / OOM / catastrophic forgetting / NaN / severe overfitting)。无消融目标。\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"N/A — experiment cancelled. DCOL failure documented in negative analysis section (Section 6.3).\\n\\nDCOL 在 6 次尝试中结构性失败：contrastive ordinal learning 在文本 depth estimation 上 缺乏将相邻 depth 分离到 embedding space 的归纳偏置。v6 (RoBERTa-large) 最稳定但仍严重 过拟合 (train 75% vs val 64.4%)，低于 RF baseline 13.7pp。失败被记录为 negative finding： \\\"Contrastive ordinal learning's inherent limitations for text depth estimation\\\"。 论文 framing 为 \\\"task formalization + systematic empirical study\\\"（非 method paper）， DCOL 失败不削弱贡献——反而支持 \\\"19 维统计特征是该问题正确抽象层级\\\" 的论点。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":387,"startLine":1,"totalLines":387}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0183CY6YRuceTYQTt6QKGZct","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — recursive_gen_depth_est\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n5\t- Backup: AAAI 2027 (abstract July 25, full paper August 1, 2026)\n6\t- EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" explicitly calls for work on data contamination, synthetic data feedback loops, and data governance — direct venue fit\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条 + Discussion implication)\n9\t\n10\t1. **Ordinal depth estimation is feasible, accurate, and robust across scales and generation modes**: Given text alone, recursive generation depth (d ∈ {0,1,2,...,K}) can be estimated with high accuracy using statistical features from reference-model perplexity distributions. On our 3-model × 3-strategy benchmark (1–1.5B), Random Forest classifiers on 19 statistical features achieve 70–85% four-class accuracy (chance=25%), with the best configuration (GPT-2 XL, temp τ=0.9) reaching 85.4%. Feature-based methods (RF, CORAL, DivEye) consistently outperform single-feature baselines across all settings. **Scale robustness**: Clean FP16 13B experiment (Qwen2.5-14B, no quantization) confirms depth signal persists at mainstream model scale, addressing the \"small model only\" concern from prior 7B QLoRA experiments. **Ecological validity**: Prompted generation experiment (topic-seeded text, not BOS-only unconditional) confirms depth signal is not an artifact of unnatural generation mode.\n11\t\n12\t2. **Depth Degradation Atlas — systematic characterization of recursive collapse** (PRIMARY): We provide the first systematic empirical characterization of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive generation depths, revealing (a) perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl) and surprisal variance (var_surprisal) as the dominant depth signal family — consistently occupying the top-4 features across all models and strategies, though their relative ranking is model-dependent, (b) non-uniform inter-depth distances (depth 0→1 gap >> depth 2→3 gap), (c) an Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable, and (d) **strategy-dependent feature trajectory reversal** — temperature sampling causes the depth-1→depth-2 feature boundary to invert relative to nucleus/top-k (cross-strategy LOO d1v2 AUC as low as 0.13), demonstrating that decoding strategy fundamentally shapes the degradation trajectory rather than merely attenuating it, and (e) **accelerated convergence mechanism** — root cause analysis confirms a genuine structural distributional shift: temperature's uniform logit scaling (vs nucleus/top-k truncation) accelerates convergence to the attractor distribution, so temp09 depth N features ≈ nucleus/topk50 depth N+1 (GPT-2 XL temp09 d1 p90_ppl median=92.2, falls into nucleus/topk50 d2 range 65–92). This is not a simple scale artifact fixable by normalization — z-score normalization improves overall LR cross-strategy accuracy (25%→61%) but does **not** recover pairwise d1v2 AUC (GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19), and does **not** improve tree-based classifiers (RF Δ<0.02pp) — confirming a distributional shift that simple feature normalization cannot resolve; whether more sophisticated domain adaptation methods could recover the d1/d2 boundary remains open. This atlas spans 3 model families × 3 decoding strategies, with scale consistency confirmed at 14B.\n13\t\n14\t3. **Cross-strategy depth estimation via two-stage pipeline + strategy-invariant signal discovery**: Naive cross-strategy transfer degrades to 59.1% with d1v2 boundary inversion. We propose a two-stage solution: (a) strategy identification classifier (57.8% — strategies share more feature space than expected), then (b) strategy-conditioned depth classifiers. The pipeline improves cross-strategy accuracy by **+11.5pp** on average (59.1% → 70.5%), with per-model results: GPT-2 XL 73.0%, OLMo 69.4%, Pythia 69.3%. Oracle ceiling at 78.3%. **Caveat**: improvement is consistent across models but absolute accuracy varies (2/3 models individually below 70%); paper must claim \"+11.5pp improvement\" rather than \"≥70% universal recovery\". The surprising finding: even with imperfect strategy routing, the pipeline works because depth signal has a **strategy-invariant core** (~60% accuracy floor) plus a strategy-specific component. This reframes cross-strategy transfer from \"broken\" to \"substantially improved with clear ceiling for future work\".\n15\t\n16\t4. **[Discussion — Practical Implication]** Depth-graduated curation as alternative to binary filtering: predicted depth provides a finer-grained quality proxy than binary real/synthetic labels, enabling graduated weighting strategies. Conceptual argument supported by depth-accuracy correlation in 3×3 matrix data; full experimental validation deferred to future work (D012).\n17\t\n18\t## Story Spine\n19\t\n20\t- **Problem**: Web-scraped training corpora increasingly contain multi-generational synthetic content from uncontrolled model→data→model feedback loops. Existing detectors answer \"is this synthetic?\" but not \"how many recursive cycles has this undergone?\" — a critical distinction since 1st-gen synthetic data can improve training while deeply recursive text drives distribution collapse.\n21\t\n22\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Binary detectors (LOKI, DivEye, Binoculars) classify real vs. synthetic but discard ordinal depth information. EditLens estimates single-pass AI editing extent but not recursive depth. Model collapse studies (Drayson et al. EMNLP 2025; Shumailov et al. Nature 2024) characterize degradation patterns but assume depth is known a priori — no method estimates depth from text alone.\n23\t\n24\t- **Our framing**: We formalize ordinal generation depth estimation as a new task, construct a multi-generational benchmark spanning 1B–14B models across 3 decoding strategies and 4 depths, and provide the first **Depth Degradation Atlas** — a systematic empirical map of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive depths, models, and strategies. The Atlas reveals (a) perplexity tail statistics as universal depth markers across all settings, (b) model-dependent strategy interaction effects with an identified root cause, and (c) the Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable. We show that feature-based classifiers achieve 70–85% four-class accuracy, and propose a two-stage strategy-aware pipeline that solves the cross-strategy deployment challenge. The depth signal persists under prompted generation (not just BOS-seeded), confirming ecological relevance.\n25\t\n26\t- **Headline result template**: \"On our multi-generational benchmark spanning model scales from 1B to 14B and 3 decoding strategies, feature-based ordinal depth estimation achieves 70–85% accuracy (chance=25%), with perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl, var_surprisal) consistently among the top-4 features across all settings. The depth signal persists under prompted (topic-seeded) generation and at 14B scale without quantization. The Depth Degradation Atlas reveals that effective discriminable depth extends to depth 3 in 7/9 settings (T=0.75). We identify strategy-dependent feature trajectory reversal and propose a two-stage pipeline that restores near within-strategy accuracy for cross-strategy deployment.\"\n27\t- **Note**: 4-class (depth 0-3) is the confirmed setting. 6-class (depth 0-5) completed via plan_011.\n28\t\n29\t## DCOL Status — Contingency Activated (D010/D011, 2026-05-15)\n30\t\n31\tDCOL v1–v5 全部失败（embedding collapse / OOM / catastrophic forgetting / 超参违规 / NaN 梯度爆炸）。\n32\t\n33\t- **Claim 2 (Atlas/EDD) 升为 PRIMARY contribution**\n34\t- **Claim 1**: Feature-based methods (RF/CORAL/DivEye) 作为 depth estimation 方法，不依赖 DCOL\n35\t- **DCOL v6 (RoBERTa-large)**: 非阻塞尝试。成功 → Section 5 bonus；失败 → negative analysis section（\"contrastive ordinal learning 在文本深度估计的固有局限\"）\n36\t- **Paper type**: Task formalization + systematic empirical study + practical framework（非 method paper）\n37\t- Atlas + EDD + feature universality + model-strategy interaction = 充分支撑 EMNLP \"New Missions\" track\n38\t\n39\t## Venue Fit Risks\n40\t\n41\t- **\"Just an empirical study\" risk**: Primary risk now that DCOL is demoted. Mitigation: (a) task formalization is a genuine contribution — no prior work estimates ordinal depth from text alone; (b) Atlas + EDD are novel analytical tools, not just tables; (c) feature universality finding (p90_ppl/var_surprisal top-4 across 9 settings) is a scientific claim with practical implications; (d) model-strategy interaction effects are a new finding; (e) **cross-strategy two-stage pipeline (Claim 3)** is a concrete practical contribution, not just analysis. EMNLP \"New Missions\" track explicitly values problem formalization.\n42\t- **Controlled vs wild gap**: Mitigation: prompted generation experiment validates signal under realistic generation conditions (topic-seeded, not BOS-only). Honest scoping — controlled setting is primary, prompted generation bridges toward ecological validity.\n43\t- **\"No novel method\" concern**: Mitigation: (a) RF/CORAL are tools, not the contribution; (b) the two-stage cross-strategy pipeline IS a novel practical method for strategy-aware depth estimation; (c) 13B clean experiment shows method scales without modification. Analogous to benchmark/analysis papers at top venues (e.g., HELM, MMLU).\n44\t- **\"Small model only\" concern**: Eliminated by clean 13B FP16 experiment. Prior 7B QLoRA results were contradictory due to quantization artifacts; 13B clean run provides definitive scale evidence.\n45\t\n46\t## Dream-Derived Requirements (D002, 2026-05-14)\n47\t\n48\t三档(best 3.0 / median 3.0 / worst 2.5)一致指出的结构性必修项：\n49\t\n50\t### 论文写作硬约束\n51\t1. **DCOL loss 描述** — 若 v6 成功：Eq.1 必须包含 attractive + repulsive 双项（N-pair formulation）。若 v6 失败：negative analysis section 描述失败模式和根因分析，无需完整 loss 公式\n52\t2. **至少4张图** — (a) AUC decay curve across depth pairs w/ EDD threshold line (b) feature trajectory panel (top-5 features × depth, stratified by model) (c) confusion matrix heatmap (d) Atlas feature×depth heatmap grid。\"Atlas without maps is a contradiction\"\n53\t3. **Bibliography 25+ references** — 必须覆盖: watermarking (Kirchenbauer ICML 2023), model collapse theory (Alemohammad ICLR 2024, Dohmatob 2024, Gerstgrasser 2024), data curation (DSIR, QuRating), multi-source attribution (Uchendu 2020), binary detectors (Binoculars Hans ICML 2024, Fast-DetectGPT Bao 2024), decoding strategy effects (Garces Arias COLING 2025, Holtzman ICLR 2020)\n54\t4. **Surprisal reference model** — 必须明确指定 reference model、说明 cross-model LOO 时如何处理、讨论 circularity\n55\t\n56\t### 指标报告硬约束\n57\t5. **d1-d5 only accuracy** — 作为 companion metric 报告，隔离 ordinal depth estimation 与 binary human-vs-machine detection\n58\t6. **EDD threshold sensitivity** — 报告 AUC threshold 在 0.65/0.70/0.75/0.80 四档下的 EDD 值\n59\t7. **k-NN inference 完整规格** — k 值、distance metric、sensitivity analysis\n60\t\n61\t### Framing 方向\n62\t8. **Atlas/EDD 为 primary contribution** — DCOL 定位为 \"one strong method within the framework\"，不作为 co-primary。三档审稿均认为 DCOL 是 incremental adaptation of CLOC。与 DCOL Contingency 一致。\n63\t9. **\"First systematic empirical map\" 需限定** — Shumailov/Drayson 已有 characterization, 我们的新颖性在 ordinal estimation lens + EDD formalization + multi-model multi-strategy coverage\n64\t\n65\t### Cross-Strategy 反转硬约束 (D015, Reviewer 降级条件)\n66\t10. **三档策略分类** — 论文不得将 nucleus 和 temperature 归为同一类 \"soft sampling\"。必须采用三档：nucleus（baseline 稳定）、temperature（信号增强但存在 d1v2 方向反转风险）、topk（信号衰减但方向一致）。D004 的 \"soft sampling\" 分组已被反转数据推翻。\n67\t11. **Discussion 必须含 per-strategy d1v2 AUC 表** — 包含 0.13/0.25 反转值 + **已确认的机制**：temperature 均匀缩放 logit（非截断）加速模型收敛到 attractor 分布（genuine structural distributional shift），temp09 depth N ≈ nucleus/topk50 depth N+1。z-score 标准化提升整体 LR 跨策略 acc（25%→61%）但**不恢复** pairwise d1v2 AUC（GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19），证实这是结构性几何偏移而非可校正的尺度差异。\n68\t12. **Limitations 必须写明跨策略部署约束** — \"跨策略部署时需先验知道目标策略类型，否则 d1/d2 预测可能反转。\"不可仅将反转作为正面发现消化。\n69\t\n70\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n71\t\n72\t1. \"EDD might be very low (depth 2-3), making the task trivial beyond shallow depths\" → Report EDD transparently; argue even low EDD is scientifically valuable (determines the boundary) and practically sufficient (shallow vs deep is the actionable distinction for curation). Data: 7/9 settings EDD≥3 at T=0.75. **Depth extension bootstrap (D027)**: 三模型 d3v4 AUC 聚集在 0.75 附近 (Pythia 0.784 p=0.001 ✅, OLMo 0.765 p=0.091 ⚠️, GPT-2 XL 0.750 p=0.505 ❌)，仅 Pythia 统计显著。**禁止**写 \"three models all achieve statistically significant EDD=4\"。正确措辞：\"d3v4 AUC consistently clusters near the 0.75 threshold (0.750–0.784) across all three models, while d4v5 AUC uniformly falls below 0.70 (0.681–0.694)\"——强调方向一致性 + 完整报告 CI 和 p-values。D024 连续衰减曲线叙事被 bootstrap 数据强力支持。\n73\t2. \"Why ordinal and not just binary?\" → d0v1 AUC=0.998 vs d1v2=0.861 vs d2v3=0.801 — ordinal structure captures monotonically decreasing but still significant discrimination at all adjacent pairs\n74\t3. \"Generalization to unseen models/strategies?\" → Cross-model LOO: mean 66.4% (holdout Pythia 62.4%, OLMo 69.2%, GPT-2 XL 67.6%) — all >chance but depth_0 recall >98% inflates headline. **Must report per-class recall** (depth_2 recall as low as 26.8%). Cross-strategy LOO: mean 59.1% (51.5–69.4%), topk50 holdout consistently worst. **temp09 holdout shows d1v2 AUC reversal** (GPT-2 XL 0.13, OLMo 0.25) — root cause confirmed as genuine structural distributional shift (temperature accelerates convergence to attractor distribution). Z-score normalization improves overall LR acc (25%→61%) but does **not** recover pairwise d1v2 AUC (GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19), confirming a distributional shift that simple feature normalization cannot resolve; whether more sophisticated domain adaptation could recover d1v2 AUC remains open. Discuss as \"strategy shapes degradation trajectory\" finding — temp09 cross-strategy d1v2 generalization remains an open problem (D013/D015/D021).\n75\t4. \"No novel method — just RF on features\" → (a) Contribution is task formalization + Atlas + EDD + systematic findings, not just method; (b) the two-stage cross-strategy pipeline (Claim 3) IS a novel practical method that solves the deployment challenge; (c) 13B clean experiment confirms the approach scales without modification. Analogous to benchmark papers (HELM, MMLU). Feature universality across 9+ settings is itself a finding.\n76\t5. \"d0 confound inflates headline metrics\" → Report d1-only accuracy alongside full accuracy; 3-class (d1/d2/d3) results already show 59–82% accuracy\n77\t6. \"EDD threshold is arbitrary\" → Sensitivity analysis at 0.65/0.70/0.75/0.80 completed (Dream D002)\n78\t7. \"No figures for Atlas\" → Minimum 4 figures (Dream D002)\n79\t8. \"Bibliography too thin\" → 25+ refs covering all relevant subfields (Dream D002)\n80\t9. \"Model-strategy interaction is just noise\" → Three-tier pattern confirmed: nucleus=stable baseline, temperature=enhances signal but reverses d1v2 feature boundary in cross-strategy transfer, topk=attenuates signal but preserves direction (D015). Garces Arias (COLING 2025) independently confirms model-dependent strategy effects.\n81\t10. \"Cross-strategy deployment is unreliable\" → **Now addressed by Claim 3**: Two-stage pipeline (strategy identification → strategy-conditioned depth classification) provides a practical solution. Strategy classifier achieves 57.8% accuracy on 19 features (below the expected >90%), indicating strategy distributions are less separable than anticipated. A two-stage pipeline (oracle strategy identification + strategy-conditioned depth classification) recovers 11.5pp over naive LOO, though practical deployment still requires either strategy metadata or improved routing. The root cause (temperature's accelerated convergence) is identified and the mechanism explained.\n82\t11. \"Signal is an artifact of unconditional BOS-seeded generation\" → Prompted generation experiment (plan_016) tests depth signal under topic-seeded generation. If signal persists → validates ecological relevance; if not → important finding about generation mode dependence (written as limitation).\n83\t12. \"Only tested on small models (1–1.5B)\" → Clean 13B FP16 experiment (Qwen2.5-14B, plan_017) confirms scale robustness without quantization confounds. Prior 7B QLoRA results were contradictory — now superseded by clean experiment.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"293a4726-1263-4b10-8462-4c709e6f178f","uuid":"033df03a-fefe-489e-966d-2e66a6021728","timestamp":"2026-05-18T16:23:49.827Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_2/projects/recursive_gen_depth_est/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T160031/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — recursive_gen_depth_est\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n- Backup: AAAI 2027 (abstract July 25, full paper August 1, 2026)\n- EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" explicitly calls for work on data contamination, synthetic data feedback loops, and data governance — direct venue fit\n\n## Core Claims (3 条 + Discussion implication)\n\n1. **Ordinal depth estimation is feasible, accurate, and robust across scales and generation modes**: Given text alone, recursive generation depth (d ∈ {0,1,2,...,K}) can be estimated with high accuracy using statistical features from reference-model perplexity distributions. On our 3-model × 3-strategy benchmark (1–1.5B), Random Forest classifiers on 19 statistical features achieve 70–85% four-class accuracy (chance=25%), with the best configuration (GPT-2 XL, temp τ=0.9) reaching 85.4%. Feature-based methods (RF, CORAL, DivEye) consistently outperform single-feature baselines across all settings. **Scale robustness**: Clean FP16 13B experiment (Qwen2.5-14B, no quantization) confirms depth signal persists at mainstream model scale, addressing the \"small model only\" concern from prior 7B QLoRA experiments. **Ecological validity**: Prompted generation experiment (topic-seeded text, not BOS-only unconditional) confirms depth signal is not an artifact of unnatural generation mode.\n\n2. **Depth Degradation Atlas — systematic characterization of recursive collapse** (PRIMARY): We provide the first systematic empirical characterization of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive generation depths, revealing (a) perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl) and surprisal variance (var_surprisal) as the dominant depth signal family — consistently occupying the top-4 features across all models and strategies, though their relative ranking is model-dependent, (b) non-uniform inter-depth distances (depth 0→1 gap >> depth 2→3 gap), (c) an Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable, and (d) **strategy-dependent feature trajectory reversal** — temperature sampling causes the depth-1→depth-2 feature boundary to invert relative to nucleus/top-k (cross-strategy LOO d1v2 AUC as low as 0.13), demonstrating that decoding strategy fundamentally shapes the degradation trajectory rather than merely attenuating it, and (e) **accelerated convergence mechanism** — root cause analysis confirms a genuine structural distributional shift: temperature's uniform logit scaling (vs nucleus/top-k truncation) accelerates convergence to the attractor distribution, so temp09 depth N features ≈ nucleus/topk50 depth N+1 (GPT-2 XL temp09 d1 p90_ppl median=92.2, falls into nucleus/topk50 d2 range 65–92). This is not a simple scale artifact fixable by normalization — z-score normalization improves overall LR cross-strategy accuracy (25%→61%) but does **not** recover pairwise d1v2 AUC (GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19), and does **not** improve tree-based classifiers (RF Δ<0.02pp) — confirming a distributional shift that simple feature normalization cannot resolve; whether more sophisticated domain adaptation methods could recover the d1/d2 boundary remains open. This atlas spans 3 model families × 3 decoding strategies, with scale consistency confirmed at 14B.\n\n3. **Cross-strategy depth estimation via two-stage pipeline + strategy-invariant signal discovery**: Naive cross-strategy transfer degrades to 59.1% with d1v2 boundary inversion. We propose a two-stage solution: (a) strategy identification classifier (57.8% — strategies share more feature space than expected), then (b) strategy-conditioned depth classifiers. The pipeline improves cross-strategy accuracy by **+11.5pp** on average (59.1% → 70.5%), with per-model results: GPT-2 XL 73.0%, OLMo 69.4%, Pythia 69.3%. Oracle ceiling at 78.3%. **Caveat**: improvement is consistent across models but absolute accuracy varies (2/3 models individually below 70%); paper must claim \"+11.5pp improvement\" rather than \"≥70% universal recovery\". The surprising finding: even with imperfect strategy routing, the pipeline works because depth signal has a **strategy-invariant core** (~60% accuracy floor) plus a strategy-specific component. This reframes cross-strategy transfer from \"broken\" to \"substantially improved with clear ceiling for future work\".\n\n4. **[Discussion — Practical Implication]** Depth-graduated curation as alternative to binary filtering: predicted depth provides a finer-grained quality proxy than binary real/synthetic labels, enabling graduated weighting strategies. Conceptual argument supported by depth-accuracy correlation in 3×3 matrix data; full experimental validation deferred to future work (D012).\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Web-scraped training corpora increasingly contain multi-generational synthetic content from uncontrolled model→data→model feedback loops. Existing detectors answer \"is this synthetic?\" but not \"how many recursive cycles has this undergone?\" — a critical distinction since 1st-gen synthetic data can improve training while deeply recursive text drives distribution collapse.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Binary detectors (LOKI, DivEye, Binoculars) classify real vs. synthetic but discard ordinal depth information. EditLens estimates single-pass AI editing extent but not recursive depth. Model collapse studies (Drayson et al. EMNLP 2025; Shumailov et al. Nature 2024) characterize degradation patterns but assume depth is known a priori — no method estimates depth from text alone.\n\n- **Our framing**: We formalize ordinal generation depth estimation as a new task, construct a multi-generational benchmark spanning 1B–14B models across 3 decoding strategies and 4 depths, and provide the first **Depth Degradation Atlas** — a systematic empirical map of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive depths, models, and strategies. The Atlas reveals (a) perplexity tail statistics as universal depth markers across all settings, (b) model-dependent strategy interaction effects with an identified root cause, and (c) the Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable. We show that feature-based classifiers achieve 70–85% four-class accuracy, and propose a two-stage strategy-aware pipeline that solves the cross-strategy deployment challenge. The depth signal persists under prompted generation (not just BOS-seeded), confirming ecological relevance.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"On our multi-generational benchmark spanning model scales from 1B to 14B and 3 decoding strategies, feature-based ordinal depth estimation achieves 70–85% accuracy (chance=25%), with perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl, var_surprisal) consistently among the top-4 features across all settings. The depth signal persists under prompted (topic-seeded) generation and at 14B scale without quantization. The Depth Degradation Atlas reveals that effective discriminable depth extends to depth 3 in 7/9 settings (T=0.75). We identify strategy-dependent feature trajectory reversal and propose a two-stage pipeline that restores near within-strategy accuracy for cross-strategy deployment.\"\n- **Note**: 4-class (depth 0-3) is the confirmed setting. 6-class (depth 0-5) completed via plan_011.\n\n## DCOL Status — Contingency Activated (D010/D011, 2026-05-15)\n\nDCOL v1–v5 全部失败（embedding collapse / OOM / catastrophic forgetting / 超参违规 / NaN 梯度爆炸）。\n\n- **Claim 2 (Atlas/EDD) 升为 PRIMARY contribution**\n- **Claim 1**: Feature-based methods (RF/CORAL/DivEye) 作为 depth estimation 方法，不依赖 DCOL\n- **DCOL v6 (RoBERTa-large)**: 非阻塞尝试。成功 → Section 5 bonus；失败 → negative analysis section（\"contrastive ordinal learning 在文本深度估计的固有局限\"）\n- **Paper type**: Task formalization + systematic empirical study + practical framework（非 method paper）\n- Atlas + EDD + feature universality + model-strategy interaction = 充分支撑 EMNLP \"New Missions\" track\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **\"Just an empirical study\" risk**: Primary risk now that DCOL is demoted. Mitigation: (a) task formalization is a genuine contribution — no prior work estimates ordinal depth from text alone; (b) Atlas + EDD are novel analytical tools, not just tables; (c) feature universality finding (p90_ppl/var_surprisal top-4 across 9 settings) is a scientific claim with practical implications; (d) model-strategy interaction effects are a new finding; (e) **cross-strategy two-stage pipeline (Claim 3)** is a concrete practical contribution, not just analysis. EMNLP \"New Missions\" track explicitly values problem formalization.\n- **Controlled vs wild gap**: Mitigation: prompted generation experiment validates signal under realistic generation conditions (topic-seeded, not BOS-only). Honest scoping — controlled setting is primary, prompted generation bridges toward ecological validity.\n- **\"No novel method\" concern**: Mitigation: (a) RF/CORAL are tools, not the contribution; (b) the two-stage cross-strategy pipeline IS a novel practical method for strategy-aware depth estimation; (c) 13B clean experiment shows method scales without modification. Analogous to benchmark/analysis papers at top venues (e.g., HELM, MMLU).\n- **\"Small model only\" concern**: Eliminated by clean 13B FP16 experiment. Prior 7B QLoRA results were contradictory due to quantization artifacts; 13B clean run provides definitive scale evidence.\n\n## Dream-Derived Requirements (D002, 2026-05-14)\n\n三档(best 3.0 / median 3.0 / worst 2.5)一致指出的结构性必修项：\n\n### 论文写作硬约束\n1. **DCOL loss 描述** — 若 v6 成功：Eq.1 必须包含 attractive + repulsive 双项（N-pair formulation）。若 v6 失败：negative analysis section 描述失败模式和根因分析，无需完整 loss 公式\n2. **至少4张图** — (a) AUC decay curve across depth pairs w/ EDD threshold line (b) feature trajectory panel (top-5 features × depth, stratified by model) (c) confusion matrix heatmap (d) Atlas feature×depth heatmap grid。\"Atlas without maps is a contradiction\"\n3. **Bibliography 25+ references** — 必须覆盖: watermarking (Kirchenbauer ICML 2023), model collapse theory (Alemohammad ICLR 2024, Dohmatob 2024, Gerstgrasser 2024), data curation (DSIR, QuRating), multi-source attribution (Uchendu 2020), binary detectors (Binoculars Hans ICML 2024, Fast-DetectGPT Bao 2024), decoding strategy effects (Garces Arias COLING 2025, Holtzman ICLR 2020)\n4. **Surprisal reference model** — 必须明确指定 reference model、说明 cross-model LOO 时如何处理、讨论 circularity\n\n### 指标报告硬约束\n5. **d1-d5 only accuracy** — 作为 companion metric 报告，隔离 ordinal depth estimation 与 binary human-vs-machine detection\n6. **EDD threshold sensitivity** — 报告 AUC threshold 在 0.65/0.70/0.75/0.80 四档下的 EDD 值\n7. **k-NN inference 完整规格** — k 值、distance metric、sensitivity analysis\n\n### Framing 方向\n8. **Atlas/EDD 为 primary contribution** — DCOL 定位为 \"one strong method within the framework\"，不作为 co-primary。三档审稿均认为 DCOL 是 incremental adaptation of CLOC。与 DCOL Contingency 一致。\n9. **\"First systematic empirical map\" 需限定** — Shumailov/Drayson 已有 characterization, 我们的新颖性在 ordinal estimation lens + EDD formalization + multi-model multi-strategy coverage\n\n### Cross-Strategy 反转硬约束 (D015, Reviewer 降级条件)\n10. **三档策略分类** — 论文不得将 nucleus 和 temperature 归为同一类 \"soft sampling\"。必须采用三档：nucleus（baseline 稳定）、temperature（信号增强但存在 d1v2 方向反转风险）、topk（信号衰减但方向一致）。D004 的 \"soft sampling\" 分组已被反转数据推翻。\n11. **Discussion 必须含 per-strategy d1v2 AUC 表** — 包含 0.13/0.25 反转值 + **已确认的机制**：temperature 均匀缩放 logit（非截断）加速模型收敛到 attractor 分布（genuine structural distributional shift），temp09 depth N ≈ nucleus/topk50 depth N+1。z-score 标准化提升整体 LR 跨策略 acc（25%→61%）但**不恢复** pairwise d1v2 AUC（GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19），证实这是结构性几何偏移而非可校正的尺度差异。\n12. **Limitations 必须写明跨策略部署约束** — \"跨策略部署时需先验知道目标策略类型，否则 d1/d2 预测可能反转。\"不可仅将反转作为正面发现消化。\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. \"EDD might be very low (depth 2-3), making the task trivial beyond shallow depths\" → Report EDD transparently; argue even low EDD is scientifically valuable (determines the boundary) and practically sufficient (shallow vs deep is the actionable distinction for curation). Data: 7/9 settings EDD≥3 at T=0.75. **Depth extension bootstrap (D027)**: 三模型 d3v4 AUC 聚集在 0.75 附近 (Pythia 0.784 p=0.001 ✅, OLMo 0.765 p=0.091 ⚠️, GPT-2 XL 0.750 p=0.505 ❌)，仅 Pythia 统计显著。**禁止**写 \"three models all achieve statistically significant EDD=4\"。正确措辞：\"d3v4 AUC consistently clusters near the 0.75 threshold (0.750–0.784) across all three models, while d4v5 AUC uniformly falls below 0.70 (0.681–0.694)\"——强调方向一致性 + 完整报告 CI 和 p-values。D024 连续衰减曲线叙事被 bootstrap 数据强力支持。\n2. \"Why ordinal and not just binary?\" → d0v1 AUC=0.998 vs d1v2=0.861 vs d2v3=0.801 — ordinal structure captures monotonically decreasing but still significant discrimination at all adjacent pairs\n3. \"Generalization to unseen models/strategies?\" → Cross-model LOO: mean 66.4% (holdout Pythia 62.4%, OLMo 69.2%, GPT-2 XL 67.6%) — all >chance but depth_0 recall >98% inflates headline. **Must report per-class recall** (depth_2 recall as low as 26.8%). Cross-strategy LOO: mean 59.1% (51.5–69.4%), topk50 holdout consistently worst. **temp09 holdout shows d1v2 AUC reversal** (GPT-2 XL 0.13, OLMo 0.25) — root cause confirmed as genuine structural distributional shift (temperature accelerates convergence to attractor distribution). Z-score normalization improves overall LR acc (25%→61%) but does **not** recover pairwise d1v2 AUC (GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19), confirming a distributional shift that simple feature normalization cannot resolve; whether more sophisticated domain adaptation could recover d1v2 AUC remains open. Discuss as \"strategy shapes degradation trajectory\" finding — temp09 cross-strategy d1v2 generalization remains an open problem (D013/D015/D021).\n4. \"No novel method — just RF on features\" → (a) Contribution is task formalization + Atlas + EDD + systematic findings, not just method; (b) the two-stage cross-strategy pipeline (Claim 3) IS a novel practical method that solves the deployment challenge; (c) 13B clean experiment confirms the approach scales without modification. Analogous to benchmark papers (HELM, MMLU). Feature universality across 9+ settings is itself a finding.\n5. \"d0 confound inflates headline metrics\" → Report d1-only accuracy alongside full accuracy; 3-class (d1/d2/d3) results already show 59–82% accuracy\n6. \"EDD threshold is arbitrary\" → Sensitivity analysis at 0.65/0.70/0.75/0.80 completed (Dream D002)\n7. \"No figures for Atlas\" → Minimum 4 figures (Dream D002)\n8. \"Bibliography too thin\" → 25+ refs covering all relevant subfields (Dream D002)\n9. \"Model-strategy interaction is just noise\" → Three-tier pattern confirmed: nucleus=stable baseline, temperature=enhances signal but reverses d1v2 feature boundary in cross-strategy transfer, topk=attenuates signal but preserves direction (D015). Garces Arias (COLING 2025) independently confirms model-dependent strategy effects.\n10. \"Cross-strategy deployment is unreliable\" → **Now addressed by Claim 3**: Two-stage pipeline (strategy identification → strategy-conditioned depth classification) provides a practical solution. Strategy classifier achieves 57.8% accuracy on 19 features (below the expected >90%), indicating strategy distributions are less separable than anticipated. A two-stage pipeline (oracle strategy identification + strategy-conditioned depth classification) recovers 11.5pp over naive LOO, though practical deployment still requires either strategy metadata or improved routing. The root cause (temperature's accelerated convergence) is identified and the mechanism explained.\n11. \"Signal is an artifact of unconditional BOS-seeded generation\" → Prompted generation experiment (plan_016) tests depth signal under topic-seeded generation. If signal persists → validates ecological relevance; if not → important finding about generation mode dependence (written as limitation).\n12. \"Only tested on small models (1–1.5B)\" → Clean 13B FP16 experiment (Qwen2.5-14B, plan_017) confirms scale robustness without quantization confounds. Prior 7B QLoRA results were contradictory — now superseded by clean experiment.\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
